><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Gambetti</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2008</year><article-title>Cell-free propagation of prion strains.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>27</volume><fpage>2557</fpage><lpage>2566</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">18800058</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000421-Westaway1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Westaway</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>DeArmond</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Cayetano-Canlas</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Groth</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Foster</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>Degeneration of skeletal muscle, peripheral nerves, and the central nervous system in transgenic mice overexpressing wild-type prion proteins.</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>76</volume><fpage>117</fpage><lpage>129</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8287472</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000421-Castilla4"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Castilla</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Gutierrez-Adan</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Brun</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Doyle</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Pintado</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Subclinical bovine spongiform encephalopathy infection in transgenic mice expressing porcine prion protein.</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><volume>24</volume><fpage>5063</fpage><lpage>5069</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15163699</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="ppat.1000421-Chiesa1"><label>13</lab